{"content":"[{\"title\":\"Streaming protocols\",\"body\":\"The Vercel AI data stream and AG-UI both ride SSE, but AG-UI carries explicit state-delta events where the AI SDK stream carries UI message parts.\",\"tags\":[\"protocol\",\"streaming\"]},{\"title\":\"Tool-call rendering\",\"body\":\"Frontends differ most in the gap between a tool being called and its result arriving — some show args streaming in, some show only a spinner.\",\"tags\":[\"ui\",\"tools\"]},{\"title\":\"Thread persistence\",\"body\":\"Client-authoritative history is the AI SDK default; the server keeps its own copy so a reload can rehydrate.\",\"tags\":[\"state\",\"persistence\"]},{\"title\":\"Generative UI\",\"body\":\"Backend-driven components are where protocols diverge: AG-UI models it natively, the AI SDK route leans on typed tool results the client maps to components.\",\"tags\":[\"ui\",\"protocol\"]}]","messageId":"#7","role":"tool","timestamp":"~","toolCallId":"#5","type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT"}
